CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=(0|10)$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
Constructing and calling a std::function whose parameter is a reference
or pointer to a class type must type-check: the converting constructor
must be selected and operator must resolve. The instantiated operator
parameter is derived from the _ArgTypes pack and must be a usable
reference type, not an unconverted frontend_pointer. std::function's
type-erased call result is not modelled, so only front-end acceptance is
checked here.
